 [(6, 1)] {'count': 1, 'bbox': (63, 0, 63, 0)} {0: -1, 7: 1} []\nCOORD 7 support (27, 3) 6 False [(6, 1)] {'count': 1, 'bbox': (63, 0, 63, 0)} {0: -1, 7: 1} []\nCOORD 7 hazard (21, 27) 6 False [(6, 1)] {'count': 1, 'bbox': (63, 0, 63, 0)} {0: -1, 7: 1} []\nCOORD 7 avatar (21, 39) 6 False [(6, 1)] {'count': 1, 'bbox': (63, 0, 63, 0)} {0: -1, 7: 1} []\nCOORD 7 wall (15, 57) 6 False [(6, 1)] {'count': 1, 'bbox': (63, 0, 63, 0)} {0: -1, 7: 1} []\nRESULT 6 196 None\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"The first experiments establish the avatar experimentally: only actions `3` and `4` translate the same 5×5 colour-9/11 object, one lattice column left/right. Coordinate action `6` is context-sensitive: empty/wall/hazard clicks are inert, a colour-12 cell changes shape, and the left colour-8 strip triggers a large gravity transition. Action `7` is inert before any selection. I’ll now isolate the post-selection behavior and test it in more than one object context."}}
